  "text": "Recipe: Vegetable Oats Cheela\nCreator: Frank Lee\nCategory: Cheela\nIngredients: 1.5 cup rolled oats, 2 Tbsp semolina, 1/2 cup gram flour (besan), salt, 1/4 tsp carom seeds, 3/4 cup water, 1 onion, 4-5 French beans, 2 green chilies, 1/2 carrot, 1/2 cup boiled & crushed green peas, 1/2 cup water, 1/4 tsp turmeric powder, Worcestershire sauce\nCooking methods: roast\nInstructions: 1.5 cup rolled oats (dry roasted for 4-5 mins), 2 Tbsp semolina (not a whole grain), 1/2 cup gram flour (besan), salt to taste, 1/4 tsp carom seeds, 3/4 cup water. Set aside for 10 mins.\n1 onion minced, 4-5 French beans minced, 2 green chilies minced. Mix in batter from Step 1. Add 1/2 carrot grated, 1/2 cup boiled & crushed green peas, 1/2 cup water, 1/4 tsp turmeric powder.\nSpread batter on non-stick griddle or pan to make a pancake (\"cheela\"). Roast both sides.\nNotes: Shared in FaceBook Group: \"SANE (Sleep, Attitude, Nutrition, Exercise) for Life\". Semolina is noted as 'not a whole grain'.",
